# CHANGE NOTES (keep newest at top):
#   2026-08-26  NEW FILE (build oa). Marketing's fresh Windows clone showed 98
#               files "modified" with identical content: the repo stores LF,
#               their machine checked out CRLF, and their git offered to commit
#               a rewrite of the entire codebase as a "fix". This file ends the
#               ambiguity FOR EVERY CLONE, present and future: text files are LF
#               in the repo AND on disk, binaries are never touched. After this
#               lands on main, a fresh clone shows a clean `git status` on any
#               machine, whatever that machine's core.autocrlf says.
#               ⚠️ NO RENORMALIZE COMMIT NEEDED: the repo already stores LF
#               (Claude's builds write LF; GitHub Desktop normalized on commit),
#               so this file only pins what is already true. If git ever offers
#               anyone a many-file line-ending commit, the answer is NO --
#               discard, pull, and ask what changed.
# =============================================================================

# Everything git detects as text: LF in the repo, LF in the working tree.
*        text=auto eol=lf

# The types this app is actually made of -- explicit, so detection never guesses.
*.py     text eol=lf
*.html   text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.css    text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.svg    text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf

# Binaries: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.mp3    binary
*.wav    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary

# I did no harm and this file is not truncated.
